{"id":"mahabharata-9-017","work":"mahabharata","part":9,"partName":"शल्यपर्व","partNameEn":"Shalya Parva","unit":17,"title":"सप्तदशोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 17 · The Madra followers fall","summary":{"en":"After Shalya's fall the seven hundred Madra chariot-followers advance but are cut down by Draupadi's sons and Satyaki. Shakuni urges the Kauravas to keep fighting, and the Pandavas drive the remnants back.","kn":"ಶಲ್ಯ ಬಿದ್ದ ನಂತರ ಏಳುನೂರು ಮದ್ರ ರಥಿಕ ಅನುಯಾಯಿಗಳು ಮುನ್ನುಗ್ಗಿ ದ್ರೌಪದೇಯರು, ಸಾತ್ಯಕಿಯಿಂದ ಕತ್ತರಿಸಲ್ಪಡುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಹೋರಾಟ ಮುಂದುವರಿಸಲು ಶಕುನಿ ಕೌರವರನ್ನು ಪ್ರೇರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಪಾಂಡವರು ಉಳಿದವರನ್ನು ಓಡಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"शल्य के गिरने पर सात सौ मद्र रथी अनुयायी आगे बढ़ते हैं पर द्रौपदेयों और सात्यकि से काट दिए जाते हैं। शकुनि कौरवों को लड़ते रहने को उकसाता है और पाण्डव बचे हुओं को पीछे हटाते हैं।","te":"శల్యుడు పడిన తరువాత ఏడు వందల మద్ర రథిక అనుచరులు ముందుకు వచ్చి ద్రౌపదేయులు, సాత్యకిచే నరకబడతారు. పోరు కొనసాగించమని శకుని కౌరవులను పురికొల్పుతాడు; పాండవులు మిగిలిన వారిని వెనక్కి తరుముతారు.","ta":"சல்யன் வீழ்ந்தபின் எழுநூறு மத்ரத் தேர்ப்பின்தொடர்வோர் முன்னேறி திரௌபதேயராலும் சாத்யகியாலும் வெட்டப்படுகின்றனர். போரைத் தொடரும்படி சகுனி கௌரவரைத் தூண்ட, பாண்டவர் எஞ்சியோரை விரட்டுகின்றனர்.","ml":"ശല്യന്റെ വീഴ്ചയ്ക്കുശേഷം, എഴുനൂറ് മദ്ര രഥയോദ്ധാക്കൾ മുന്നോട്ടുവരുന്നു; എന്നാൽ ദ്രൗപദിയുടെ പുത്രന്മാരും സാത്യകിയും അവരെ വെട്ടിവീഴ്ത്തുന്നു. കൗരവർ പൊരുതിത്തുടരാൻ ശകുനി പ്രേരിപ്പിക്കുന്നു; പാണ്ഡവർ ശേഷിച്ചവരെ പിന്നോട്ടോടിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 9.17; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jun 23 2020","sections":[{"title":"शल्यपर्व","titleEn":"Shalya Parva","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"शल्ये तु निहते राजन्मद्रराजपदानुगाः ।\nरथाः सप्तशता वीरा निर्ययुर्महतो बलात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Shalya had been slain, O king, seven hundred brave chariot-warriors who had followed the king of the Madras rushed out in great force."}},{"n":2,"text":"दुर्योधनस्तु द्विरदमारुह्याचलसंनिभम् ।\nछत्रेण ध्रियमाणेन वीज्यमानश्च चामरैः ।\nन गन्तव्यं न गन्तव्यमिति मद्रानवारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana, mounted on an elephant like a mountain, with an umbrella held over him and fans waving, tried to stop the Madras, crying, \"Do not go, do not go!\""}},{"n":3,"text":"दुर्योधनेन ते वीरा वार्यमाणाः पुनः पुनः ।\nयुधिष्ठिरं जिघांसन्तः पाण्डूनां प्राविशन्बलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though Duryodhana held them back again and again, those heroes, eager to kill Yudhishthira, plunged into the Pandava army."}},{"n":4,"text":"ते तु शूरा महाराज कृतचित्ताः स्म योधने ।\nधनुःशब्दं महत्कृत्वा सहायुध्यन्त पाण्डवैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those brave men, O great king, with their minds set on battle, twanged their bows loudly and fought together with the Pandavas."}},{"n":5,"text":"श्रुत्वा तु निहतं शल्यं धर्मपुत्रं च पीडितम् ।\nमद्रराजप्रिये युक्तैर्मद्रकाणां महारथैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that Shalya was dead and that the son of Dharma was hard pressed, the great chariot-fighters of the Madras, devoted to their king's cause, went on the attack."}},{"n":6,"text":"आजगाम ततः पार्थो गाण्डीवं विक्षिपन्धनुः ।\nपूरयन्रथघोषेण दिशः सर्वा महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Arjuna, the son of Pritha, came up, shaking his bow Gandiva and filling all the directions with the rumble of his chariot."}},{"n":7,"text":"ततोऽर्जुनश्च भीमश्च माद्रीपुत्रौ च पाण्डवौ ।\nसात्यकिश्च नरव्याघ्रो द्रौपदेयाश्च सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna and Bhima, the two sons of Madri, Satyaki the tiger among men, and all the sons of Draupadi gathered round."}},{"n":8,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्नः शिखण्डी च पाञ्चालाः सह सोमकैः ।\nयुधिष्ठिरं परीप्सन्तः समन्तात्पर्यवारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhrishtadyumna and Shikhandi, with the Panchalas and Somakas, surrounded Yudhishthira on every side to protect him."}},{"n":9,"text":"ते समन्तात्परिवृताः पाण्डवैः पुरुषर्षभाः ।\nक्षोभयन्ति स्म तां सेनां मकराः सागरं यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Encircled by the Pandavas, those bulls among men threw that army into turmoil, as sea-monsters churn the ocean."}},{"n":10,"text":"पुरोवातेन गङ्गेव क्षोभ्यमाना महानदी ।\nअक्षोभ्यत तदा राजन्पाण्डूनां ध्वजिनी पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the great river Ganga is stirred by an east wind, so the Pandava host was churned up again then, O king."}},{"n":11,"text":"प्रस्कन्द्य सेनां महतीं त्यक्तात्मानो महारथाः ।\nवृक्षानिव महावाताः कम्पयन्ति स्म तावकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your warriors, great chariot-fighters careless of their lives, charged into the vast army and shook it as mighty winds shake trees."}},{"n":12,"text":"बहवश्चुक्रुशुस्तत्र क्व स राजा युधिष्ठिरः ।\nभ्रातरो वास्य ते शूरा दृश्यन्ते नेह केचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Many shouted, \"Where is King Yudhishthira? And where are his brothers? Not one of those heroes is to be seen here!\""}},{"n":13,"text":"पाञ्चालानां महावीर्याः शिखण्डी च महारथः ।\nधृष्टद्युम्नोऽथ शैनेयो द्रौपदेयाश्च सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Where are the mighty Panchalas, the great chariot-fighter Shikhandi, Dhrishtadyumna, Satyaki and all the sons of Draupadi?\""}},{"n":14,"text":"एवं तान्वादिनः शूरान्द्रौपदेया महारथाः ।\nअभ्यघ्नन्युयुधानश्च मद्रराजपदानुगान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As they spoke so, the great chariot-fighters, the sons of Draupadi, together with Yuyudhana, struck down the followers of the king of the Madras."}},{"n":15,"text":"चक्रैर्विमथितैः केचित्केचिच्छिन्नैर्महाध्वजैः ।\nप्रत्यदृश्यन्त समरे तावका निहताः परैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the battle your men were seen slain by the enemy, some with wheels shattered, some with great banners cut down."}},{"n":16,"text":"आलोक्य पाण्डवान्युद्धे योधा राजन्समन्ततः ।\nवार्यमाणा ययुर्वेगात्तव पुत्रेण भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the Pandavas all around in the fight, O king, your warriors rushed away swiftly, though your son tried to hold them back, O Bharata."}},{"n":17,"text":"दुर्योधनस्तु तान्वीरान्वारयामास सान्त्वयन् ।\nन चास्य शासनं कश्चित्तत्र चक्रे महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana tried to stop those heroes with soothing words, but none of the great chariot-fighters there obeyed his command."}},{"n":18,"text":"ततो गान्धारराजस्य पुत्रः शकुनिरब्रवीत् ।\nदुर्योधनं महाराज वचनं वचनक्षमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Shakuni, son of the king of Gandhara, skilled in speaking, said to Duryodhana, O great king:"}},{"n":19,"text":"किं नः संप्रेक्षमाणानां मद्राणां हन्यते बलम् ।\nन युक्तमेतत्समरे त्वयि तिष्ठति भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Why is the army of the Madras being slaughtered while we look on? This is not right in battle, O Bharata, while you stand by.\""}},{"n":20,"text":"सहितैर्नाम योद्धव्यमित्येष समयः कृतः ।\nअथ कस्मात्परानेव घ्नतो मर्षयसे नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"We agreed that we would fight together. Why then do you tolerate the enemy killing our own men, O king?\""}},{"text":"दुर्योधन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana said:"}},{"n":21,"text":"वार्यमाणा मया पूर्वं नैते चक्रुर्वचो मम ।\nएते हि निहताः सर्वे प्रस्कन्नाः पाण्डुवाहिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I held them back before, but they did not heed my word. These men, having charged the Pandava army, are all being killed.\""}},{"text":"शकुनिरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Shakuni said:"}},{"n":22,"text":"न भर्तुः शासनं वीरा रणे कुर्वन्त्यमर्षिताः ।\nअलं क्रोद्धुं तथैतेषां नायं काल उपेक्षितुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Angry warriors in battle do not obey their lord's command. This is no time to be angry with them or to neglect them.\""}},{"n":23,"text":"यामः सर्वेऽत्र संभूय सवाजिरथकुञ्जराः ।\nपरित्रातुं महेष्वासान्मद्रराजपदानुगान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let us all go there together, with horses, chariots and elephants, to rescue the mighty archers who followed the king of the Madras.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"अन्योन्यं परिरक्षामो यत्नेन महता नृप ।\nएवं सर्वेऽनुसंचिन्त्य प्रययुर्यत्र सैनिकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"O king, let us protect one another with great effort.\" Having thought it over in this way, they all went to where the soldiers were."}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":25,"text":"एवमुक्तस्ततो राजा बलेन महता वृतः ।\nप्रययौ सिंहनादेन कम्पयन्वै वसुंधराम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed, the king, surrounded by a great force, set out, shaking the earth with lion-roars."}},{"n":26,"text":"हत विध्यत गृह्णीत प्रहरध्वं निकृन्तत ।\nइत्यासीत्तुमुलः शब्दस्तव सैन्यस्य भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Strike! Pierce! Seize! Attack! Cut them down!\" Such was the tumultuous cry of your army, O Bharata."}},{"n":27,"text":"पाण्डवास्तु रणे दृष्ट्वा मद्रराजपदानुगान् ।\nसहितानभ्यवर्तन्त गुल्ममास्थाय मध्यमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandavas, seeing the followers of the Madra king gathered together, turned against them, taking up a central formation."}},{"n":28,"text":"ते मुहूर्ताद्रणे वीरा हस्ताहस्तं विशां पते ।\nनिहताः प्रत्यदृश्यन्त मद्रराजपदानुगाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Within a moment, O lord of the people, those Madra followers were seen cut down in hand-to-hand fighting."}},{"n":29,"text":"ततो नः संप्रयातानां हतामित्रास्तरस्विनः ।\nहृष्टाः किलकिलाशब्दमकुर्वन्सहिताः परे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, as we advanced, our triumphant foes, who had destroyed their enemies, raised joyful shouts all together."}},{"n":30,"text":"अथोत्थितानि रुण्डानि समदृश्यन्त सर्वशः ।\nपपात महती चोल्का मध्येनादित्यमण्डलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Headless trunks were seen rising up all around, and a great meteor fell across the disc of the sun."}},{"n":31,"text":"रथैर्भग्नैर्युगाक्षैश्च निहतैश्च महारथैः ।\nअश्वैर्निपतितैश्चैव संछन्नाभूद्वसुंधरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The earth was covered with broken chariots, shattered yokes and axles, slain great chariot-fighters and fallen horses."}},{"n":32,"text":"वातायमानैस्तुरगैर्युगासक्तैस्तुरंगमैः ।\nअदृश्यन्त महाराज योधास्तत्र रणाजिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Warriors were seen on that battlefield, with horses galloping like the wind or tangled in their yokes."}},{"n":33,"text":"भग्नचक्रान्रथान्केचिदवहंस्तुरगा रणे ।\nरथार्धं केचिदादाय दिशो दश विबभ्रमुः ।\nतत्र तत्र च दृश्यन्ते योक्त्रैः श्लिष्टाः स्म वाजिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some horses dragged chariots with broken wheels; some, carrying half a chariot, wandered off in all ten directions; and elsewhere horses were seen bound up in their harness."}},{"n":34,"text":"रथिनः पतमानाश्च व्यदृश्यन्त नरोत्तम ।\nगगनात्प्रच्युताः सिद्धाः पुण्यानामिव संक्षये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Charioteers were seen falling, O best of men, like perfected beings dropping from the sky when their merit is spent."}},{"n":35,"text":"निहतेषु च शूरेषु मद्रराजानुगेषु च ।\nअस्मानापततश्चापि दृष्ट्वा पार्था महारथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the heroes who followed the Madra king were slain and the great Pandava warriors saw us advancing,"}},{"n":36,"text":"अभ्यवर्तन्त वेगेन जयगृध्राः प्रहारिणः ।\nबाणशब्दरवान्कृत्वा विमिश्राञ्शङ्खनिस्वनैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"they charged swiftly, eager for victory and hard-hitting, making the din of bowstrings mingled with the sound of conches."}},{"n":37,"text":"अस्मांस्तु पुनरासाद्य लब्धलक्षाः प्रहारिणः ।\nशरासनानि धुन्वानाः सिंहनादान्प्रचुक्रुशुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having found us again, those strikers, their aim sure, shook their bows and roared like lions."}},{"n":38,"text":"ततो हतमभिप्रेक्ष्य मद्रराजबलं महत् ।\nमद्रराजं च समरे दृष्ट्वा शूरं निपातितम् ।\nदुर्योधनबलं सर्वं पुनरासीत्पराङ्मुखम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, seeing the great Madra army slain and the brave king of the Madras felled in battle, all of Duryodhana's force turned its back once more."}},{"n":39,"text":"वध्यमानं महाराज पाण्डवैर्जितकाशिभिः ।\nदिशो भेजेऽथ संभ्रान्तं त्रासितं दृढधन्विभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck down by the Pandavas, flushed with victory, O great king, the bewildered army fled in all directions, terrified by those firm archers."}}]}]}